.TH ARCH\-MAP 1 "2026-09" "arch-map" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
arch-map \- a living C4-style container diagram from real infrastructure
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B arch-map
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Builds a C4-style architecture diagram from infrastructure that actually
exists, rather than from a drawing kept by hand: Terraform state, a live
Kubernetes namespace, or both at once.
.PP
The output is Mermaid by default, which renders natively on GitHub, so the
diagram can live in the repository and be regenerated instead of redrawn.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-tfstate " FILE"
Terraform state JSON: either a state file, or the output of
.BR "terraform show \-json" .
.TP
.BI \-\-k8s " NAMESPACE"
Read live workloads, services and ingresses from this namespace via
.BR kubectl .
.TP
.BI \-o " FILE" ", " \-\-output " FILE"
Write here instead of standard output.
.TP
.BI \-\-title " TITLE"
Diagram title.
.TP
.BI \-\-level " LEVEL"
.BR context ,
.B container
(default) or
.BR component .
Context collapses to one box per kind; container and component show every
discovered node.
.TP
.BI \-\-format " FORMAT"
Diagram syntax; the default is
.BR mermaid .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
A diagram was produced.
.TP
.B non-zero
No source was given, or a source could not be read.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
From Terraform state:
.PP
.RS
.B arch-map \-\-tfstate terraform.tfstate \-o ARCHITECTURE.md
.RE
.PP
From a live namespace:
.PP
.RS
.B arch-map \-\-k8s payments
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR terraform (1),
.BR kubectl (1).
Project documentation:
https://github.com/fabiocicerchia/arch-map
